# Text is stored and checked out with LF. With no .gitattributes and no
# core.autocrlf set, the bytes a contributor commits are the bytes stored, so
# an editor that writes CRLF mixes endings into the tree without anything
# reporting it -- ruff-format and basedpyright are both indifferent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# rollups.csv and included_labels.csv under sagemaker/configs/ are generator
# output: scripts/generate_training_config.py opens them with newline="" and
# writes through csv.writer, whose excel dialect terminates rows with CRLF.
# Normalising them would be undone by the next run, so git leaves their bytes
# as committed. configs/example/ holds header-only stubs written by hand.
sagemaker/configs/**/rollups.csv         -text
sagemaker/configs/**/included_labels.csv -text
